            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac rhythm problems in subarachnoid haemorrhage: report of two patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>211-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients were admitted with the provisional diagnosis of ischaemic heart disease. Both patients had lumbar punctures and the final diagnosis of subarachnoid haemorrhage with complicating cardiac arrhythmias was made in both cases.</AbstractText>
